I chose these weights to approximate a proportional‑derivative controller using the available state features.  
- `params[0]` (cart position) is set to zero to avoid a constant bias on the force.  
- `params[1]` and `params[2]` (sin θ₁, sin θ₂) receive strong negative gains (‑2.0) so that any deviation from the upright position (sin θ≈0) produces a corrective force opposite to the tilt.  
- `params[3]` and `params[4]` (cos θ₁, cos θ₂) are given positive gains (2.0) and the bias `params[9]` is set to –4.0, which cancels the constant term when the pendulum is perfectly upright (cos θ≈1). This creates a zero‑force equilibrium at the target state.  
- `params[5]` (cart velocity) and `params[6]`, `params[7]` (angular velocities) have modest negative gains (‑0.5, ‑1.5, ‑1.5) providing damping to reduce oscillations and prevent chattering.  
